# Phase 20/23 — Cloudflare Pages headers (STATIC ASSETS ONLY).
#
# SCOPE: this deployment ships `dist/_worker.js`, so Cloudflare Pages serves
# dynamic routes (every SSR HTML document, every /_serverFn RPC response, the
# sitemap) from the Worker. Cloudflare applies `_headers` rules ONLY to
# responses from the static asset store — Worker-generated responses bypass
# this file completely. Verified on the live deployment: GET /about returned
# NO CSP and NO HSTS despite this file existing.
#
# That is why the SSR security headers AND the CSP live in
# src/lib/security-headers.ts and are applied in `src/server.ts`, which every
# Worker response funnels through. Do NOT rely on this file to protect HTML
# documents.
#
# CSP — Phase 23 UPDATE (the Phase 20 "DO NOT ENABLE" block is RESOLVED):
# The original blocker was that TanStack Start's SSR stream emits inline
# <script> tags for hydration with no `nonce`, so `script-src 'self'` broke
# hydration. TanStack Router exposes a supported per-request option for exactly
# this — `createRouter({ ssr: { nonce } })` — which is threaded into React's
# renderToReadableStream, the $_TSR bootstrap, the $tsr-stream-barrier tag,
# <Scripts> and <HeadContent> (including the <meta property="csp-nonce"> the
# client re-reads during hydration).
#
# src/server.ts now generates one crypto-random nonce per HTTP response, runs
# the request inside an AsyncLocalStorage scope so src/router.tsx's getRouter()
# reads it, and writes the SAME value into the Content-Security-Policy header.
# The enforcing policy therefore needs NO 'unsafe-inline' in script-src and no
# 'unsafe-eval' at all. 'unsafe-inline' appears ONLY in style-src, because
# `sonner` and Radix's react-remove-scroll-bar inject <style> elements at
# runtime with no nonce hook — see src/lib/security-headers.ts (CSP_EVIDENCE).
#
# DO NOT paste the SSR CSP into this file. A static file cannot carry a
# per-request nonce, and the `script-src 'self'` variant that would fit here is
# exactly the policy that broke hydration. The Worker-emitted policy is the one
# that protects documents.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/guides/preview
  Cache-Control: private, no-store
